"commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2022-01-28T08:31:33Z","performed_via_github_app":null},{"id":5969034670,"node_id":"SE_lADOAGuhRc5CePrTzwAAAAFjyD2u","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/events/5969034670","actor":{"login":"KotlinIsland","id":65446343,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NDQ2MzQz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65446343?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KotlinIsland","html_url":"https://github.com/KotlinIsland","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KotlinIsland/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KotlinIsland/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KotlinIsland/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KotlinIsland/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KotlinIsland/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KotlinIsland/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KotlinIsland/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KotlinIsland/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KotlinIsland/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"subscribed","commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2022-01-28T08:31:33Z","performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/comments/1024879816","html_url":"https://github.com/python/mypy/issues/12076#issuecomment-1024879816","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/12076","id":1024879816,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAGuhRc49FmzI","user":{"login":"kreathon","id":12074878,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMDc0ODc4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12074878?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kreathon","html_url":"https://github.com/kreathon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kreathon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kreathon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kreathon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kreathon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kreathon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kreathon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kreathon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kreathon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kreathon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-01-29T09:57:15Z","updated_at":"2022-01-29T09:57:15Z","body":"I am not sure if this is a bug or a missing features.\r\n\r\nThe [documentation](https://mypy.readthedocs.io/en/stable/common_issues.html#ignoring-a-whole-file) states only to use `type: ignore` to ignore the whole module (without any specific error code). That also matches with the code (I just looked it up):\r\n\r\n```\r\n# A \"# type: ignore\" comment before the first statement of a module\r\n# ignores the whole module:\r\nif (ismodule and stmts and self.type_ignores\r\n        and min(self.type_ignores) < self.get_lineno(stmts[0])):\r\n    self.errors.used_ignored_lines[self.errors.file][min(self.type_ignores)].append(\r\n        codes.MISC.code)\r\n    block = Block(self.fix_function_overloads(self.translate_stmt_list(stmts)))\r\n    mark_block_unreachable(block)\r\n    return [block]\r\n```\r\n\r\n(Note that I am not a mypy developer, so I might be wrong)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/comments/1024879816/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"kreathon","id":12074878,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMDc0ODc4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12074878?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kreathon","html_url":"https://github.com/kreathon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kreathon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kreathon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kreathon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kreathon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kreathon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kreathon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kreathon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kreathon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kreathon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/comments/1065977572","html_url":"https://github.com/python/mypy/issues/12076#issuecomment-1065977572","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/12076","id":1065977572,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAGuhRc4_iYbk","user":{"login":"Zeckie","id":49095968,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5MDk1OTY4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49095968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zeckie","html_url":"https://github.com/Zeckie","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zeckie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zeckie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zeckie/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zeckie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zeckie/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zeckie/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zeckie/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zeckie/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zeckie/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-03-12T22:38:41Z","updated_at":"2022-03-12T22:38:41Z","body":"It is ignoring the supplied error code, and treating it as though it is just `# type: ignore`, pretty much the opposite of what the error message says.\r\n\r\nExample showing that it ignores errors with a different code:\r\nhttps://mypy-play.net/?mypy=latest&python=3.10&flags=show-error-codes%2Cstrict%2Cwarn-unused-ignores&gist=a864a4660d66062af67f85f49e89096f\r\n\r\n[The documentation](https://mypy.readthedocs.io/en/stable/type_inference_and_annotations.html?highlight=ignore#silencing-type-errors) currently says:\r\n> ... you can also ignore all mypy checks in a file, by adding a `# type: ignore` at the top of the file:\r\n\r\nAnd on [a different page](https://mypy.readthedocs.io/en/stable/error_codes.html#silencing-errors-based-on-error-codes):\r\n> You can use a special comment `# type: ignore[code, ...]` to only ignore errors with a specific error code (or codes) on a particular line. This can be used even if you have not configured mypy to show error codes. Currently it’s only possible to disable arbitrary error codes on individual lines using this comment.\r\n\r\nThe best solution would be to add support for error codes on ignores at the top of a file, to ignore all errors of that code in the whole file.  \r\n\r\nIf that isn't possible, I think it should give an error more like (whether used with `--warn-unused-ignores` or not): \r\n```\r\ntest.py:1: error: Error code not supported on file level ignore\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/comments/1065977572/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"Zeckie","id":49095968,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5MDk1OTY4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49095968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zeckie","html_url":"https://github.com/Zeckie","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zeckie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zeckie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zeckie/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zeckie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zeckie/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zeckie/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zeckie/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zeckie/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zeckie/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/comments/1066002974","html_url":"https://github.com/python/mypy/issues/12076#issuecomment-1066002974","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/12076","id":1066002974,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAGuhRc4_ieoe","user":{"login":"KotlinIsland","id":65446343,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NDQ2MzQz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65446343?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KotlinIsland","html_url":"https://github.com/KotlinIsland","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KotlinIsland/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KotlinIsland/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KotlinIsland/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KotlinIsland/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KotlinIsland/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KotlinIsland/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KotlinIsland/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KotlinIsland/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KotlinIsland/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-03-13T01:49:02Z","updated_at":"2022-07-04T03:14:05Z","body":"Put this at the top of the file and you will get the desired behavior:\r\n```py\r\n# mypy: allow-untyped-defs\r\n```\r\n[playground](https://mypy-play.net/?mypy=latest&python=3.10&flags=strict&gist=e85d8fa5b55d3c4a6c84d4cbbb9a883d)\r\nIt's using a feature called [inline configuration](https://mypy.readthedocs.io/en/stable/inline_config.html)\r\n\r\n\r\nThe following doesn't work (invalid module level config), but is silently ignored due to #12342:\r\n```py\r\n# mypy: disable-error-code=no-untyped-def\r\n```","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/comments/1066002974/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"KotlinIsland","id":65446343,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NDQ2MzQz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65446343?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KotlinIsland","html_url":"https://github.com/KotlinIsland","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KotlinIsland/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KotlinIsland/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KotlinIsland/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KotlinIsland/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KotlinIsland/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KotlinIsland/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KotlinIsland/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KotlinIsland/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KotlinIsland/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"id":6311286887,"node_id":"LE_lADOAGuhRc5CePrTzwAAAAF4Lphn","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/events/6311286887","actor":{"login":"AlexWaygood","id":66076021,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2